          "replacement_region_source": "// SAFETY: `switch_signal` points to `length * bitmap_len` bytes from the caller;\n// `length` is the explicit L1 length source and is stable in this region; the\n// function's unsafe contract provides non-null valid storage; and this shared\n// slice is the only reference created to that backing memory here.\nlet switch_signal_view = unsafe {\n    core::slice::from_raw_parts(\n        switch_signal,\n        length.wrapping_mul(bitmap_len) as usize,\n    )\n};\n// SAFETY: `block_id` points to `length` bytes from the caller; `length` is the\n// explicit L1 length source and is stable in this region; the function's unsafe\n// contract provides non-null valid storage; and this mutable slice is the only\n// reference created to that backing memory here.\nlet block_id_view = unsafe { core::slice::from_raw_parts_mut(block_id, length as usize) };\n\nwhile byte_ix > 0 as size_t {\n    let mask_0: uint8_t = ((1 as c_uint) << (cur_id as c_int & 7 as c_int)) as uint8_t;\n    byte_ix = byte_ix.wrapping_sub(1);\n    ix_0 = (ix_0 as c_ulong).wrapping_sub(bitmap_len as c_ulong) as size_t as size_t;\n    let switch_ix = ix_0.wrapping_add((cur_id as c_int >> 3 as c_int) as size_t) as usize;\n    let block_ix = byte_ix as usize;\n    if unsafe { *switch_signal_view.get_unchecked(switch_ix) } as c_int & mask_0 as c_int != 0 {\n        let prev_id = unsafe { *block_id_view.get_unchecked(block_ix) };\n        if cur_id as c_int != prev_id as c_int {\n            cur_id = prev_id;\n            num_blocks = num_blocks.wrapping_add(1);\n        }\n    }\n    unsafe {\n        *block_id_view.get_unchecked_mut(block_ix) = cur_id;\n    }\n}\nreturn num_blocks;",
          "rule_id": "III④"
        }
